#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements {#requirements}"
msgstr "Prérequis {#requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "QRMI supports the following operating systems (OS): \n"
msgstr "QRMI prend en charge les systèmes d'exploitation (OS) suivants :\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compiling environment {#compiling-environment}"
msgstr "Environnement de compilation {#compiling-environment}"

#. type: Bullet: '*  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "[Rust compiler](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) 1.91 or above\n"
msgstr ""
"[Compilateur Rust](https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install) 1.91 ou "
"supérieur\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A C compiler: for example, GCC (`gcc`) on Linux and Clang (`clang-tools-"
"extra`) for Rust unknown targets/cross compilations. QRMI is compatible with"
" a compiler conforming to the C11 standard\n"
msgstr ""
"Un compilateur C : par exemple, GCC (`gcc`) sous Linux et Clang (`clang-"
"tools-extra`) pour les cibles inconnues de Rust / compilations croisées. "
"QRMI est compatible avec un compilateur conforme à la norme C11\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`make/cmake` (make/cmake RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "`make/cmake` (RPM make/cmake pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`openssl` (openssl-devel RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "`openssl` (RPM openssl-devel pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "`zlib` (zlib-devel RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "`zlib` (RPM zlib-devel pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Python 3.11, 3.12, or 3.13 (For Python API)\n"
msgstr "Python 3.11, 3.12 ou 3.13 (pour l'API Python)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Libraries and header files needed for Python development (python3.1x-devel "
"RPM for RHEL-compatible OS):\n"
msgstr ""
"Bibliothèques et fichiers d'en-tête nécessaires au développement Python (RPM"
" python3.1x-devel pour les OS compatibles RHEL) :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "/usr/include/python3.1x\n"
msgstr "/usr/include/python3.1x\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "/usr/lib64/libpython3.1x.so\n"
msgstr "/usr/lib64/libpython3.1x.so\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Doxygen (for generating C API documentation), depending on the OS:\n"
msgstr "Doxygen (pour générer la documentation de l'API C), selon l'OS :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```dnf install doxygen``` for Linux (RHEL/CentOS/Rocky Linux and others)\n"
msgstr ""
"```dnf install doxygen``` pour Linux (RHEL/CentOS/Rocky Linux et autres)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "```apt install doxygen``` for Linux (Ubuntu and others)\n"
msgstr "```apt install doxygen``` pour Linux (Ubuntu et autres)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "```brew install doxygen```for MacOS\n"
msgstr "```brew install doxygen```pour MacOS\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Runtime environment {#runtime-environment}"
msgstr "Environnement d'exécution {#runtime-environment}"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "gcc (libgcc RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "gcc (RPM libgcc pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "openssl (openssl-libs RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "openssl (RPM openssl-libs pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "zlib (zlib RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr "zlib (RPM zlib pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Libraries and header files needed for Python development (python3.1x-devel "
"RPM for RHEL-compatible OS)\n"
msgstr ""
"Bibliothèques et fichiers d'en-tête nécessaires au développement Python (RPM"
" python3.1x-devel pour les OS compatibles RHEL)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build the Rust/C API library with the following commands wherever you have "
"saved the QRMI repository.\n"
msgstr ""
"Compile la bibliothèque API Rust/C avec les commandes suivantes, à l'endroit"
" où tu as sauvegardé le dépôt QRMI.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To build the Python package, first set up a Python environment and install "
"the required dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour compiler le paquet Python, commence par configurer un environnement "
"Python et installer les dépendances requises.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create the stub files for the Python code.\n"
msgstr "Crée les fichiers stub pour le code Python.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, build the Python wheels for distribution to your hosts.\n"
msgstr "Enfin, compile les wheels Python pour les distribuer sur tes hôtes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The wheel is created in the `./target/release/maturin/wheels` directory. You"
" can distribute and install on your hosts by `pip install <wheel>`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le wheel est créé dans le répertoire `./target/release/maturin/wheels`. Tu "
"peux le distribuer et l'installer sur tes hôtes avec `pip install "
"<wheel>`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging {#logging}"
msgstr "Journalisation {#logging}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"QRMI supports [log crate](https://crates.io/crates/log) for logging. You can"
" find the detailed QRMI runtime logs by specifying `RUST_LOG` environment "
"variable with the log level. Supported levels are `error`, `warn`, `info`, "
"`debug`, and `trace`. The default level is `warn`. \n"
msgstr ""
"QRMI prend en charge le [crate log](https://crates.io/crates/log) pour la "
"journalisation. Tu peux consulter les journaux détaillés d'exécution de QRMI"
" en spécifiant la variable d'environnement `RUST_LOG` avec le niveau de "
"journalisation. Les niveaux pris en charge sont `error`, `warn`, `info`, "
"`debug` et `trace`. Le niveau par défaut est `warn`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "If you specify `trace`, you can find underlying HTTP transaction logs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tu spécifies `trace`, tu peux consulter les journaux de transactions HTTP"
" sous-jacentes.\n"

